# Fixed 2026-11-23, defect 2679, lane-p255-impl (panel 255's R1, route C):
# libpng, where the defect was found. A decode that fails jumps by libpng's
# own `longjmp` to the `jmp_buf` of its `png_struct`, which is then freed; the
# next decode saves into the next struct.
# Symptom: `--sanitize`: heap-use-after-free at the runtime's
# `hero_jmp_fingerprint` on the second decode, the read of the freed struct's
# buffer (Linux arm64 and Darwin, panel 255, 2026-11-22).
# Cause: the runtime read a fingerprint of every buffer a save filled at the
# thread's next save point or jump, by which time libpng had given it back.
# Fix: a jump reads one word of the buffer it jumps to, which the C library
# reads next; no buffer a save filled is read at any other moment (route C).
# A machine without libpng skips the case, which `package` tells
# (`ffi_package`).
extern "fixedbugs-2679-libpng.h" pkgconfig "libpng"
    function png_make() -> i64
    function png_decode(which: i64) -> i64

function main()
    print(png_make())
    print(png_decode(which: 0))
    print(png_decode(which: 1))
    print(png_decode(which: 0))
